'' '..NAME( )' OVER A NAME THAT IS BOTH A TYPE AND A PROCEDURE is the procedure, as a bare
'' identifier in expression position is. The Windows headers declare 'type
'' INITCOMMONCONTROLSEX' beside 'InitCommonControlsEx', and AfxNova's CWindow constructor
'' calls '..InitCommonControlsEx( @icc )'. The '..' lookup took whichever symbol the slot held
'' first -- the TYPE -- so the call statement was dropped (every CWindow skipped the
'' common-controls initialisation) and the assignment form was refused with TKO0738.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/global-qual-call-type-name.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0738
